      m_Calls: []
  m_text: "Chapter 2 | The Handmaiden: Escape\n\nOn the surface, The Handmaiden is
    an elegant con. Underneath, it is a rehearsal for escape. Inside a structure
    built on control, authorship, and possession, Sook-hee keeps pushing open doors\u2014pulling
    herself out of someone else\u2019s script. The first time she stayed out past
    midnight in New York became inseparable from this film, like a marker in her
    own timeline: a moment when she understood that leaving isn\u2019t shameful\u2014leaving
    is a skill. She once brought him to Metrograph, but he didn\u2019t like it, couldn\u2019t
    understand it, and refused even basic respect. She didn\u2019t expect perfect
    empathy for her taste, but the absence of respect was enough to reveal a red
    flag. So for her, The Handmaiden isn\u2019t only a favorite movie. It\u2019s
    a reminder card: she can escape at any time, and she can lift herself out of
    the wrong kind of relationship."
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
  m_fontAsset: {fileID: 11400000, guid: fb31704cec070074ca40032b135cceca, type: 2}
